     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">     My first guess would be scaling of common factors. You set first loadings for fac1_17, fac2_17 and fac4_17 to be &quot;NA&quot;--that is, to be free parameters--and you specified <a href=\"http://std.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792418224713000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2baUaMNcapjPFhWsf9VgKX\">std.lv</a>=F, so you are not standardizing your common factors. You must either constrain loadings or fix factor variances (OK, or use the effects coding option), or a factor model is not identified. I believe, if you remove the NA modifiers, or remove the <a href=\"http://std.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792418224713000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2baUaMNcapjPFhWsf9VgKX\">std.lv</a>=F option, the model will be identified.</div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
