     3,
     "<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thursday, 3 March 2022 at 13:37:34 UTC <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">edward...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">     My first guess would be scaling of common factors. You set first loadings for fac1_17, fac2_17 and fac4_17 to be &quot;NA&quot;--that is, to be free parameters--and you specified <a href=\"http://std.lv\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792418224728000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3RoGusN-mWmjXHinPt9s7G\">std.lv</a>=F, so you are not standardizing your common factors. You must either constrain loadings or fix factor variances (OK, or use the effects coding option), or a factor model is not identified. I believe, if you remove the NA modifiers, or remove the <a href=\"http://std.lv\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792418224728000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3RoGusN-mWmjXHinPt9s7G\">std.lv</a>=F option, the model will be identified.</div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Mar 3, 2022 at 7:37 AM Laura Havers &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">lhav...@mail.bbk.ac.uk</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>Hi all,</div><div><br></div><div>Can anyone help me spot what the source of this NPD warning is?? (ps, I&#39;m aware of the limitations of using single-item indicators, many thanks)<br></div><div><br></div><div> 2: In lav_object_post_check(object) :</div>  lavaan WARNING: covariance matrix of latent variables<br>                is not positive definite;<br><div>                use lavInspect(fit, &quot;<a href=\"http://cov.lv\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cov.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792418224728000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ZGncrDNU7isDg-hcq8HlP\">cov.lv</a>&quot;) to investigate.</div><div><br></div><div>model &lt;- <br>  &#39;fac1_17 =~ NA*pcl2prnd121 + pcl2prnd141 + pcl2prnd111 + pcl2prnd011 + pcl2prnd041 + pcl2prnd151<br>fac2_17 =~ NA*pcl2prnd091 + pcl2prnd081 + pcl2prnd071 + pcl2prnd051 + pcl2prnd061<br>fac3_17 =~ 1*pcl2prnd031<br>fac4_17 =~ NA*pcl2prnd021 + pcl2prnd131<br>fac5_17 =~ 1*pcl2prnd101<br>fac1_17 ~~ 1*fac1_17<br>fac2_17 ~~ 1*fac2_17<br>fac4_17 ~~ 1*fac4_17<br>pcl2prnd101 ~~ 0*pcl2prnd101<br>pcl2prnd031 ~~ 0*pcl2prnd031&#39;</div><div>fit_model &lt;- cfa(model, data=data, estimator = &quot;MLR&quot;, <a href=\"http://std.lv\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792418224728000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3RoGusN-mWmjXHinPt9s7G\">std.lv</a>=F, missing = &quot;fiml&quot;) <br></div><div><br></div><div>&gt; lavInspect(fit_model, &quot;<a href=\"http://cor.lv\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cor.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792418224728000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0NtBwD9YqtM0ggNfSWpvRm\">cor.lv</a>&quot;)<br>        fc1_17 fc2_17 fc3_17 fc4_17 fc5_17<br>fac1_17 1.000                             <br>fac2_17 0.868  1.000                      <br>fac3_17 0.579  0.724  1.000               <br>fac4_17 0.813  0.987  0.711  1.000        <br>fac5_17 0.848  0.802  0.533  0.684  1.000 </div><div><br></div><div>&gt; parameterEstimates(fit_model)</div>           lhs op         rhs   est    se       z pvalue ci.lower ci.upper<br>1      fac1_17 =~ pcl2prnd121 0.745 0.042  17.862      0    0.663    0.827<br>2      fac1_17 =~ pcl2prnd141 0.737 0.040  18.464      0    0.659    0.